2. Vendor and Supplier Registry

The vendor side should use the same level of discipline.

That includes subcontractors, mechanics, fuel suppliers, tire shops, parts vendors, equipment rental, waste facilities, water sources, towing/recovery, lodging, labs, training providers and any other company LeaseOS pays or relies upon.

Vendor record	Examples

Vendor ID	VEN-000392
Legal/payee name	Who receives payment
Operating name	Public/company name
Vendor class	disposal, fuel, mechanic, subcontractor, parts, training etc.
Tax information	GST/HST/PST registration where applicable
Banking/payment profile	Protected accounting fields
Remittance address	AP
Primary contacts	Accounting/operations/emergency
Insurance	certificates + expiration
WCB/workers-comp documentation	where applicable
Licence/permit documents	relevant vendor qualifications
Rate sheets	current/historical
Purchase-order requirements	yes/no + rules
Approved-vendor status	pending/approved/suspended/blocked
Safety status	orientation/prequalification
Contract	MSA/service agreement
Service areas	geographic coverage
Vendor scorecard	service, pricing, incidents, late paperwork
Documents	invoices, tickets, statements, contracts


Vendor approval should be separate from simply creating the vendor.

That gives you:

created → pending verification → approved → suspended → archived

and makes it impossible for a clerk accidentally to pay an unapproved entity without an authorized override.


