3. Unified Client–Vendor Relationship Model

Some companies can be both.

A disposal company might purchase transportation services from you while also charging you disposal fees. Another trucking company might subcontract work to you while performing subcontract work for you.

So don't make the database assume:

> company = customer OR vendor



Instead:

> organization
→ client relationship
→ vendor relationship
→ facility relationship
→ subcontractor relationship



That keeps one legal organization record while allowing multiple commercial roles.

This will prevent duplicate records like:

ABC Oil Ltd.
ABC OIL
ABC Oilfield
A.B.C. Oil Ltd

from becoming four accounting entities.

LeaseOS should have duplicate detection using business number, normalized company name, address, phone and email domain.


