4. Accounts Receivable — Client Money

Every billable job should eventually produce an auditable AR chain:

Client → Contract → Rate Sheet → PO → Job → Dispatch → Trip → Load → Ticket → Signed Evidence → Charge Calculation → Invoice → Payment → Reconciliation

Each invoice line should preserve the source used to calculate it.

Example:

Invoice 10482

Line:

> Unit 216 — hydrovac transportation — Sept 16 — 11.5 hours — $185/hr



should link directly to:

job

driver

unit

client

approved rate

time events

signed field ticket

client signoff

GPS evidence if permitted

adjustments

tax treatment

invoice


Then the office doesn't have to explain later how $2,127.50 appeared.

LeaseOS should be able to show:

CALCULATION RECEIPT

11.50 h × $185.00 = $2,127.50

with the rate version and evidence used.


