The most important design rule

I would make LeaseOS use source-linked accounting, not traditional free-form office bookkeeping alone.

A clerk should not normally type:

> $4,330 disposal expense



and walk away.

LeaseOS should know:

> $4,330 disposal expense
came from Vendor VEN-0092
Invoice D-39828
for five accepted manifests
under Job J-2026-1842
matching scale tickets A–E
approved by Manager 014
paid under transaction PAY-9284.



That is the difference between an ordinary trucking office program and the kind of auditable operating system LeaseOS is becoming.

I would make this a formal new LeaseOS tranche called something like Commercial Office / Accounting Records Chain, and build it in phases: organization registry → client/vendor records → PO/rates → manifests/disposal → AR/AP → tax ledger → document registry → audit packages → office dashboard.